      "writtenOn": "2026-10-13T15:01:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 818: 🔴 `admitSipRequest()` classifies any in-dialog `OPTIONS` carrying `X-Jami-Handover-Request` as a recovery probe for caller-side calls, even when it arrives on the currently active channel and without validating generation/channel transition. This lets a peer (or delayed/replayed probe traffic) trigger unnecessary recovery restarts on an already healthy channel, causing avoidable media churn and call instability. Restrict probe admission to requests coming from a non-active candidate channel and require a valid/matching handover generation before returning `Probe`; otherwise treat it as normal `OPTIONS` (`Accept`) or reject as stale.",
      "revId": "8afb3f1e28e4339f4b236daef86a82e5c16f8fa4",
